The doctor dashboard was mixing web-specific font settings instead of using the same typography as the mobile app. This updates the dashboard shell, related doctor-facing views, and the `MyHealthPal` logo to render with the same DM Sans family.

- **Typography source of truth**
  - Added local DM Sans font loading in the DoctorAPP root layout.
  - Switched the shared sans/font variables to DM Sans so dashboard text inherits one consistent family.

- **Dashboard-wide font consistency**
  - Updated the existing shared font utility to resolve to DM Sans without renaming downstream class usage.
  - Preserved compatibility for components still referencing the older `--font-poppins` variable by aliasing it to the new shared font stack.

- **Logo alignment**
  - The `MyHealthPal` gradient logo now inherits the same dashboard font stack, so branding matches the rest of the doctor UI.

- **Representative change**
  ```tsx
  import "@fontsource/dm-sans/400.css";
  import "@fontsource/dm-sans/500.css";
  import "@fontsource/dm-sans/600.css";
  import "@fontsource/dm-sans/700.css";
  ```

  ```css
  :root {
    --font-dm-sans: "DM Sans", "Segoe UI", Arial, sans-serif;
    --font-poppins: var(--font-dm-sans);
  }

  .font-poppins {
    font-family: var(--font-poppins), "DM Sans", sans-serif;
  }
  ```

