`ScoreGauge` called `score.toFixed(1)` without guaranteeing `score` is a JS `number`. When the LLM returns `"overall_score": "8.5"` (string) instead of `8.5` (number), the `?? 0` guard passes it through, causing `TypeError: score.toFixed is not a function` and a blank tab.

## Changes

- **`ScoreGauge.tsx`** — coerce at the source: `const numericScore = Number(score) || 0`; add `?? statusColor.fail` fallback for unrecognised status strings
- **`GovernanceTab.tsx`**
  - `normalizeStatus()` helper lowercases + validates status strings from the LLM (`"Pass"` / `"PASS"` / `"pass"` → `"pass"`)
  - `Array.isArray` guards on all list fields (`checks`, `missing_information`, `contradictions`, `risk_flags`) so an unexpected object shape never reaches `.map()`
  - Per-check `score` coerced via `Number(check?.score ?? 0) || 0`

```ts
// Before — crashes when LLM returns a string
const pct = Math.min(score / maxScore, 1);
// …
<span>{score.toFixed(1)}</span>  // TypeError if score === "8.5"

// After
const numericScore = Number(score) || 0;
const pct = Math.min(numericScore / maxScore, 1);
// …
<span>{numericScore.toFixed(1)}</span>
```

